    "type": "paragraph",
    "bbox": [
      47.99,
      397.0,
      420.08,
      475.67
    ],
    "reading_order": 15,
    "text": "Solution : We are given that ABCD is a parallelogram.\nSo, we deduce that all the properties that hold for a\nparallelogram hold for ABCD. Therefore, in particular,\nthe property that ‘the opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal to each other’, holds.\nSince  we know AD = 5 cm, we can deduce that BC = 5 cm. Similarly, we deduce that\nDC = 7 cm.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
